+
+  <hr>
+  <h2 id=Protected>Protected buffers</h2>
+  <p>
+  Buffers can be marked as protected.
+  w3m will refuse to remove protected buffers from the buffer stack
+  and warn about their presence when exiting.
+  Protected buffers are indicated by a leading bang.
+  Protection status can be toggled either by the command <code>PROTB</code>
+  or via the buffer stack menu.
+  Prepending any URL with a bang will also mark the corresponding buffer as protected.
+  To treat a leading bang as literal escape it with a backslash
+  (<code>w3m '\!file'</code>).
+  </p>
